Source: Paul Littlewood. "The last round of the Robert Silk international
chess tourna­ment in London yesterday was sternly contested, and it took
seven and a half hours continuous play before the last game between Littlewood
and Speelman was decided. Had Littlewood won, he would have been first alone,
but in the end he had to concede that the rook and pawn ending was a draw."
The Times (Golombek), 16 July 1976} 1/2-1/2

